{
  "_": "harken's screenshots (.github/screens/apps.md; which phones it is on is flake.nix's list, `publish`): its server is server.sh (the demo's catalogue as a media root its scanner reads), signed in to as `user`, who goes by `name`. `walk`: the phones' and the larger screens' (the same list), walked inside the app from a new install (ui/docs/shots.md, \"In the App\"): `welcome`, the first run's page; then signed in through the first run, landing on Home; and every shot after reached by tapping from where the last left it, each step naming an element by its id (`tab:library`, `library.show:albums`, `library.open-album:<title>`; a shot's `<id>.tree.txt` lists them). `player` plays the album open from its page's Play, grows the now-playing bar into the full player (`shell.open-player`, the accessory's own press) and pauses it there, so the picture holds still; `queue` puts up its queue from the full player's Queue row; `settings` puts it back and opens Settings from who is signed in. `wide`: the wide windows' one walk, by the same ids in the same order on all three (.github/screens/apps.md, \"The wide windows\"): the desktop's iced window (app-desktop.sh, ui/rust/shots: signed in straight back from the run's dev server), the browser's page (app-web.sh, web-shots.js: the page published as the demo, `web.demo`) and the Mac's own window (app-mac.sh: the demo's library, `mac`), each at `window` (`scale` the desktop's pixels), light then dark, each step taken inside the app by its id (`ark_app::shots`: ArkHost's on the Mac, as the iPhone's walk; the page's `window.arkShots`; the desktop's window's). The demo of the Mac and the browser is on the run's day (DEMO_DAY), else `today`. What one platform alone can do is a narrow addition, said by `on`: a shot or a step `on` some of `desktop`, `web` and `mac` is taken there alone (the browser's command box, opened in a page of its own by its address, `query`, as arkui-web reads it). `mac` is the Mac's own launch arguments, and `welcome` its first run's page, opened with no demo before the walk.",
